.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt TR 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm tr
.Nd translate, delete, or squeeze characters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cCds
.Ar set1
.Op Ar set2
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read standard input and write the transformed characters to standard output.
With two sets, translate characters from
.Ar set1
to the corresponding characters of
.Ar set2 .
A short second set repeats its last character.
Sets accept literals, ranges and character classes such as
.Ql [:lower:]
and
.Ql [:upper:] .
.Pp
.Fl d
deletes characters in the first set.
.Fl s
squeezes repeated output characters in the selected set.
.Fl c
and
.Fl C
complement the first set.
Quote sets that contain shell metacharacters or spaces.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
This is the unmodified sbase 0.1 implementation from the pinned archive,
using its UTF-8 rune routines, not locale-dependent collation.
It opens no files and uses only its inherited input and output streams.
GNU-specific options are not provided.
No filesystem, process or kernel interface is added by this port.
Host reference cases and ABSD ELF checks are distinct from guest execution;
see
.Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, nonzero for invalid options, missing operands, invalid sets
or stream errors.
Diagnostics use standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/bin/echo "first hour" | tr a-z A-Z
/bin/echo a123b | tr -d 0-9
/bin/echo "two  spaces" | tr -s " "
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cut 1 ,
.Xr sed 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
